Great — everything works and fills the screen. A few observations:

1. MENU: title 荣耀王者 123px tall at font 92 (font min 368x123). Good (96px level, measured label height 123). Buttons 640×96 except host (740 due to text). IP row present. Right column content vertically centered — buttons at y=427..755, status/hint at 849..971, so group occupies 427-971, centered in 40..1360 (center 700; group center ~699). 

2. The left brand panel: desc at y=288, then version label at y=1308 — big whitespace in between, as required ("下面留白，底部放版本/状态行"). Good.

3. ROOM: left 1450 (64.9% of 2232), rows/font. Right 782: 开始选人 button at y=119 near top — hmm, the right column layout: st label at 58, button at 119, then spacer, foot at 1158, leave at 1245. So button near top. That looks acceptable ("右侧状态/开始按钮列"), though maybe better vertically centered like menu. Not critical.

Roster label height 953 with min height 43; it expands (empty text). Good.

4. SELECT: hero list 760×751, middle 1092, right 380; bottom confirm 680×92 (measured 680×96 because row height from button min 96? min is 680x92 but actual 96 — because the leave button 640x96 sets row height 96 and buttons fill vertically. Fine.)

Hero cards: 176×62 with 2 per row? Wait in the hero panel width 760, cards at x=78 and next... Only "吕布" printed per row, meaning flow width ~700 gives 3 columns of 176+8 = 552; should fit 3. Hmm each printed button y increments 70 (62+8) and only one per row printed? Looking at output: 吕布 (78,421), 亚瑟 (78,491), 铠 (78,561)... They're each in their own row! That's because HFlowContainer width is small? The flow is inside hero_box (VBox in ScrollContainer 760 wide, content width ~ 760-28-... = 718). HFlowContainer min width? HFlowContainer inside VBox: VBox sets child width to container width, so flow width ~718 → should fit 3 cards of 176 = 528+16. But output shows single column. Why?

Ah — because ScrollContainer with horizontal_scroll_mode = DISABLED: the hero_box gets width = scroll width only if the ScrollContainer's child has size_flags_horizontal = EXPAND? In ScrollContainer, if horizontal scrolling disabled, child width = scroll width. But VBoxContainer hero_box's minimum width = max child min width. HFlowContainer's minimum width = ? HFlowContainer's min width is the width of the widest child (176), and it doesn't wrap until given width. When VBox gives it width = 718, flow should lay out 3 per row. But observed 1 per row → flow got width ~176.

Hmm wait: maybe HFlowContainer's min size reports the sum? Actually, output shows y increments exactly 70 = 62+8 (v_separation 8), with same x=78. So each flow row has 1 item, i.e. flow width < 352. Since the label "战士（6）" is 110 wide, flow is a sibling. Let me check: in the old code, was it multiple per row? The old flow had same structure, main width 820. Perhaps HFlowContainer in a VBox inside a ScrollContainer doesn't expand because ScrollContainer sizes child to its min size when horizontal scroll disabled? In Godot 4, ScrollContainer sets child size to max(min_size, scroll size) for the axis where scrolling is disabled... Actually `ScrollContainer` with horizontal mode disabled → child width = container width (I believe it forces child size to viewport width). Hmm.

Hmm, but the observed geometry: hero panel 760, ScrollContainer inside with width 718, hero_box child. The cards x=78: panel at 64 + pad 14 = 78. So hero_box x=78 and each card at x=78 width 176 → flow width 176. That suggests hero_box width = 176 (its min width) rather than 718. Which means ScrollContainer did not stretch child horizontally. Because hero_box's size_flags_horizontal default FILL — in ScrollContainer, child is sized to max(child min, container size) for disabled axes? I recall ScrollContainer sets child rect size based on its minimum size and only expands to fill if... Let me recall Godot source: `ScrollContainer::_reposition_children()`:

```
if (horizontal_scroll_mode == SCROLL_MODE_DISABLED) {
    r.size.width = MAX(r.size.width, ofs.x + ...);
}
```
Hmm. Actually implementation:
```
Size2 child_min_size = c->get_combined_minimum_size();
if (child_min_size.width > size.width || ...) 
```
Let me just look: In Godot 4 `ScrollContainer::_reposition_children()`:
```
if (is_layout_rtl()) ...
for each child:
    r.position = -scroll_ofs ...
    if (h_scroll_mode != SCROLL_MODE_DISABLED) r.size.width = MAX(r.size.width /* from child get_size? */)
```
I recall: `
if (horizontal_scroll_mode == SCROLL_MODE_DISABLED) {
    r.size.width = MAX(child_min.x, size.width);
}
` Hmm that would give 718.

But observed otherwise. Maybe the old panel had width 820 and cards 150 wide with... old output unknown. Wait — maybe HFlowContainer's min width is large (sum of first row?) Godot HFlowContainer min size = size of largest child? If HFlowContainer reports min width = sum of all children in one line? No.

Hmm, but the key clue: cards x=78 for all, and hero_panel width 760. Also 吕布 at y=421; 战士 label at y=378 h=33 → 378+33+10 gap = 421 ✓. Then 亚瑟 at 491 = 421+62+8. So flow rows each 1 card.

Why would flow be 176 wide? HFlowContainer's minimum size — Godot's HFlowContainer::get_minimum_size() returns `ThemeDB...`? It computes min size as max child min size for width, and height of a single line. So min width 176, min height 62 (one line). Then when placed in VBox, the VBox gives it full width 718. Unless... the VBox width itself is 176.

Then hero_box width would be 176 → meaning ScrollContainer child width = its min width (176-ish, considering role hrow label 110). The 战士 label at x=94 = 78+? hrow has bar 6 + sep 10 → label x = 78+6+10 = 94 ✓, and label size 110 (min). So hero_box width = 176 → yes, ScrollContainer didn't stretch the child.

